@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "What is Azure DevOps?";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure DevOps is a cloud-based suite of development and collaboration tools provided by Microsoft. It offers a complete DevOps toolchain for developing, deploying, and managing software projects efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-4">
        <p>
            Azure DevOps enables teams to automate workflows, enhance collaboration, and accelerate software delivery. It provides tools for **version control, continuous integration, continuous deployment (CI/CD), agile project management, and testing**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h2>Key Features of Azure DevOps</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>End-to-End DevOps Tools:</strong> Supports the entire software development lifecycle (SDLC), from planning to deployment.</li>
                <li><strong>CI/CD Automation:</strong> Enables seamless integration and automated deployment using Azure Pipelines.</li>
                <li><strong>Flexible & Scalable:</strong> Works with any programming language, platform, and external tools.</li>
                <li><strong>Integrated Security:</strong> Provides built-in compliance and security features to safeguard code and infrastructure.</li>
                <li><strong>Cloud & On-Prem Deployment:</strong> Supports hybrid models, allowing deployments on Azure, AWS, or on-premises.</li>
                <li><strong>Collaboration & Agile Management:</strong> Offers powerful tools for work tracking, sprint planning, and team coordination.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/overview/azure-devops-overview.png" alt="Azure DevOps Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps provides an integrated toolchain for DevOps workflows.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Core Services of Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>Azure DevOps consists of several key services that help teams build and deliver software efficiently:</p>
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Azure Boards</h4>
                <p>Agile work tracking with Kanban, Scrum, and dashboards.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Azure Repos</h4>
                <p>Git-based version control for efficient source code management.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Azure Pipelines</h4>
                <p>CI/CD pipelines for automating builds, tests, and deployments.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row align-items-center mt-3">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <h4>Azure Test Plans</h4>
                <p>Comprehensive test management for quality assurance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <h4>Azure Artifacts</h4>
                <p>Package management for secure storage and sharing of dependencies.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Benefits of Using Azure DevOps</h2>
        <table class="table table-bordered text-center mt-3">
            <thead class="table-dark">
                <tr>
                    <th>Benefit</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Faster Software Delivery</strong></td>
                    <td>Automates deployments and reduces time-to-market.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Enhanced Collaboration</strong></td>
                    <td>Brings teams together with shared workflows and tools.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Scalability</strong></td>
                    <td>Works for startups to enterprise-level organizations.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Security & Compliance</strong></td>
                    <td>Integrates security policies into development workflows.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps is a powerful, all-in-one platform that streamlines software development and deployment. With features like CI/CD, version control, agile planning, and security integration, it enables teams to build high-quality applications efficiently.
        </p>
        <p>
            By adopting Azure DevOps, organizations can improve **collaboration, speed, and reliability** in their development processes, ensuring continuous delivery of software solutions.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntroductionToMicrosoftAzure", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Introduction to Microsoft Azure</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("KeyAzureDevOpsServices", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Key Azure DevOps Services &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>